  <Patch Id="FJzZkKqVfW12i9kQk6L0hz">
    <Canvas Id="N0E8bKG5vqG1aLaGsfcogC" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pt4eKK7Ag0dikcitT4Vmar">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="T1yChjTcVpcQLJ4rxMEL44">
        <Canvas Id="VxYLn5bECvkjhyGerEE3sc" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VaZNqihOnpwz6dORWEdpu0" Bounds="60,30,620,160" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="01 - Change how the world looks.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ONE KNOB. Everything this map is made of - every road, every coastline, every colour - arrives as&#xD;&#xA;small square pictures from a server, and WHICH server is the string in URL Template. Change it and&#xD;&#xA;the whole world changes appearance. Nothing else in this patch has to move.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Switch Enabled on first. It starts off because opening a document in vvvv RUNS it, and a map that&#xD;&#xA;fetched the moment you opened it would give you no chance to decline.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;PASTE ANY OF THESE OVER THE URL, one at a time, and put the credit next to it on Attribution:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  https://tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png&#xD;&#xA;      Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, SRTM | Style: (c) OpenTopoMap (CC-BY-SA)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png&#xD;&#xA;      (c) OpenStreetMap contributors&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  https://a.tile-cyclosm.openstreetmap.fr/cyclosm/{z}/{x}/{y}.png&#xD;&#xA;      (c) OpenStreetMap contributors | CyclOSM          (zoom in - it is built for street level)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  https://tiles.maps.eox.at/wmts/1.0.0/s2cloudless-2020_3857/default/g/{z}/{y}/{x}.jpg&#xD;&#xA;      EOxCloudless 2020 by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2020)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Look at that last one twice. The placeholders are in a different ORDER - z, y, x - and it still&#xD;&#xA;works, because only their presence matters, not their arrangement. It is also a photograph rather&#xD;&#xA;than a drawing, which is a difference you can see and nobody has to name for you.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ATTRIBUTION IS A PIN, NOT AN AFTERTHOUGHT. Almost every tile service requires credit ON THE MAP,&#xD;&#xA;and a layer carrying none contributes nothing to the Attribution widget. Filling it in is the&#xD;&#xA;difference between complying and appearing to.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TWO BASEMAPS THAT WORK PERFECTLY AND ARE NOT ALLOWED, which is the more useful lesson: CARTO&apos;s&#xD;&#xA;(their own licence restricts the tile service to enterprise customers) and Esri&apos;s World Imagery&#xD;&#xA;(granted only for tracing features). Both return a correct, good-looking tile if you ask.&#xD;&#xA;A REQUEST THAT SUCCEEDS TELLS YOU NOTHING ABOUT WHETHER YOU WERE ALLOWED TO MAKE IT.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT TO WATCH:&#xD;&#xA;  Layers Built  should reach 1 and stay. It counts rebuilds. If it climbs frame after frame,&#xD;&#xA;                CLOSE VVVV - every rebuild starts a fresh round of tile requests, and that once&#xD;&#xA;                exhausted a machine of ephemeral ports and took a home network down.&#xD;&#xA;  Cache Status  where the tiles are kept, and how much. Only tiles you actually looked at are&#xD;&#xA;                stored, which is what OpenStreetMap&apos;s tile policy asks for.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THIS PATCH USES ONE PACKAGE, VL.Mapsui, which is normally a reason to live in that package&apos;s own&#xD;&#xA;help folder rather than here. It is the exemption written into this pack&apos;s rules: a course with a&#xD;&#xA;hole at chapter 1 is worse than a node appearing in two places.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHERE TO GO NEXT - three different directions, no order:&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 02        put your own shapes on it&#xD;&#xA;  Prompt Two colours only     how little can a map be made of and still read?&#xD;&#xA;  Prompt Out of this world    no basemap at all. Invent the place.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="RLpAbpo7mNE2DqvCX5EEBI" Comment="URL Template" Bounds="-660,340,640,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="https://tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="TcGRKPbSPuBuztmr9GW8Ep" Comment="Attribution" Bounds="-660,375,640,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, SRTM | Style: (c) OpenTopoMap (CC-BY-SA)">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="UnaIkq8cPr0a4UZQVn7ji7" Comment="Enabled" Bounds="79,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="false">
